### Planner API — worked examples
### Run the first request, then the rest pick up {{token}} automatically.
### Works in VS Code (REST Client) and Rider/Visual Studio .http files.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@owner = owner@planner.local
@password = PlannerOwner123!

### 1. Sign in
# @name signIn
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=planner-desktop&username={{owner}}&password={{password}}&scope=openid profile email roles offline_access planner.api

@token = {{signIn.response.body.access_token}}
@refresh = {{signIn.response.body.refresh_token}}

### 2. Who am I, and which teams am I in
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Refresh the access token
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id=planner-desktop&refresh_token={{refresh}}

### 4. Teams
# @name teams
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

@teamId = {{teams.response.body.$[0].id}}

### 5. Board columns for that team
# @name states
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams/{{teamId}}/states
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

@todoState = {{states.response.body.$[1].id}}
@doneState = {{states.response.body.$[4].id}}

### 6. Team members
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Create a team (admin only) — its default states and your lead membership come with it
POST {{host}}/api/v1/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "OPS",
  "name": "Operations",
  "description": "Runs the on-prem installation.",
  "color": "#4CB782"
}

### 8. Projects, with their issue rollup
# @name projects
GET {{host}}/api/v1/projects?teamId={{teamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

@projectId = {{projects.response.body.items[0].id}}

### 9. Create a project
POST {{host}}/api/v1/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}",
  "name": "Q4 hardening",
  "summary": "Close out the reliability backlog before the holiday freeze.",
  "status": "Planned",
  "health": "OnTrack",
  "targetDate": "2026-12-15"
}

### 10. Milestones of a project
# @name milestones
GET {{host}}/api/v1/projects/{{projectId}}/milestones
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

@milestoneId = {{milestones.response.body.$[0].id}}

### 11. Add a milestone
POST {{host}}/api/v1/projects/{{projectId}}/milestones
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Release candidate",
  "description": "Feature complete, bugs only.",
  "targetDate": "2026-11-30"
}

### 12. Project documentation
POST {{host}}/api/v1/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "title": "Deployment runbook",
  "content": "# Deployment\n\n1. `docker compose pull`\n2. `docker compose up -d`\n3. Watch `/health/ready`."
}

### 13. Documents attached to a project
GET {{host}}/api/v1/projects/{{projectId}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. The board: one team, ordered exactly as it renders
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues?teamId={{teamId}}&sort=board&pageSize=200
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Create an issue
# @name newIssue
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}",
  "title": "Reconnect banner flickers on a slow network",
  "description": "Debounce the visibility toggle by 500ms.",
  "priority": "High",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "milestoneId": "{{milestoneId}}",
  "estimate": 2,
  "dueDate": "2026-09-30"
}

@issueId = {{newIssue.response.body.id}}
@issueKey = {{newIssue.response.body.key}}

### 16. PATCH one field — everything else is untouched
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priority": "Urgent" }

### 17. PATCH an explicit null — this clears the field
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "estimate": null, "assigneeId": null }

### 18. Drag to another column
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/move
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stateId": "{{doneState}}" }

### 19. Look it up the way a person refers to it
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues/by-key/{{issueKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. Comment
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Reproduced on a 3G profile — debounce looks right." }

### 21. Attach a link or a file reference (metadata only)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileName": "network-trace.har",
  "storageUri": "file:///srv/planner/attachments/network-trace.har",
  "contentType": "application/json",
  "sizeBytes": 148213
}

### 22. Sub-issue
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}",
  "title": "Add the debounce helper",
  "parentId": "{{issueId}}"
}

### 23. Filters: OR within a field, AND across fields
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues?teamId={{teamId}}&priority=Urgent&priority=High&stateType=Started&sort=priority
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Free-text search (trigram over title and description)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues?teamId={{teamId}}&search=reconnect
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Delta sync after being offline
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues?teamId={{teamId}}&updatedSince=2026-08-27T00:00:00Z&includeArchived=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. History of one issue
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/activity
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 27. Team-wide activity feed
GET {{host}}/api/v1/activity?teamId={{teamId}}&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28. Archive rather than delete
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 29. Create a user (admin only)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dana@example.local",
  "password": "CorrectHorseBattery1",
  "displayName": "Dana Developer",
  "role": "member"
}

### 30. Directory search, for an assignee picker
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users?search=dana
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 31. Health
GET {{host}}/health/ready
